@namespace Showcase.Web.Client.Pages

@page "/fa-login-form/api"

<DemoPageHeader Title="Login Form: API" ComponentName="FaLoginForm" DocSlug="fa-login-form" />

<ComponentSubNav BaseRoute="/fa-login-form" />

<div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="fa-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Type</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td><code>OnSubmit</code></td><td><code>EventCallback&lt;FaLoginRequest&gt;</code></td><td>required — FaLoginForm never calls an auth endpoint itself, this is where you do</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>ShowRememberMe</code></td><td><code>bool</code></td><td>default <code>true</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>Busy</code></td><td><code>bool</code></td><td>disables submit, swaps its text to "Logging in…" — flip this around your own <code>OnSubmit</code> await</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>ErrorText</code></td><td><code>string?</code></td><td>set from your own <code>OnSubmit</code> handler to show a failed-login message</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>UsernameLabel</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td>default <code>"Username"</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>PasswordLabel</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td>default <code>"Password"</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>SubmitText</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td>default <code>"Log in"</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>FooterContent</code></td><td><code>RenderFragment?</code></td><td>extra content between the fields and the submit button — a "Forgot password?" link, a sign-up link, etc.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>CssClass</code></td><td><code>string?</code></td><td></td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>
<p>No <code>AdditionalAttributes</code> splat on this component — every attribute you set is one of the above. Plain HTML form + native inputs, not <code>EditForm</code>-based — there's no model for a caller to own.</p>
